BT /F1 10 Tf 40 750 Td 13 TL (Position: Senior Data Scientist / Machine Learning Engineer) ' (Company: CloudScale AI Technologies) ' (Location: Remote / Hybrid) ' (ABOUT THE ROLE:) ' (We are seeking a talented Data Scientist to join our enterprise AI engineering team. In this role, you will build production-grade machine learning models, natural language processing applications, and data analytics pipelines.) ' (KEY RESPONSIBILITIES:) ' (- Design, train, and evaluate predictive machine learning models and deep learning architectures.) ' (- Implement NLP and text analysis models to process unstructured enterprise data.) ' (- Build robust data pipelines and perform statistical data analysis on terabyte-scale datasets.) ' (- Deploy and monitor AI services on cloud infrastructure using Docker, Kubernetes, and Amazon Web Services \(AWS\) or Google Cloud Platform \(GCP\).) ' (- Work closely with engineering teams in an Agile scrum environment to integrate models into production REST API services.) ' (- Present data-driven insights and interactive dashboards using Power BI or Tableau.) ' (REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS & SKILLS:) ' (- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Statistics, or related technical field.) ' (- 3+ years of hands-on experience in Python, SQL, and data analysis.) ' (- Strong proficiency in Machine Learning frameworks: Scikit-Learn, PyTorch, or TensorFlow.) ' (- Experience with Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) or Computer Vision techniques.) ' (- Solid experience with relational databases such as PostgreSQL or MySQL.) ' (- Experience with containerization \(Docker, Kubernetes\) and CI/CD pipelines.) ' (- Familiarity with cloud environments: Amazon Web Services \(AWS\) or Microsoft Azure.) ' (- Experience with business intelligence tools: Power BI or Tableau.) ' (- Strong problem solving, communication, and collaboration skills.) ' ET
